# L2: ROUND TIMES and D0's rate, audits off (the timing profiles; the times are the design's P(n) and F, so an audit's cost must not be in
# them). The gate's round-timing plan, five arms:
#   padded-4k, padded-32k   c2-packed-tp4-time-gate       four users whose answers end one after another (600 / 1,200 / 1,800 / 2,400
#                                                          tokens, every stream to its budget): the rounds run at 4, 3, 2 and 1 live users,
#                                                          so ONE boot gives P(4), P(3), P(2) (the padded and full 64-row block) and the
#                                                          lone user on today's per-request engines, at 4,096 and at 32,768 context
#   base-lone-4k            c2-packed-tp4-time-gate       four real-text users one at a time on the per-request engines (the baseline)
#   d0-lone-4k, d0-lone-32k c2-packed-tp4-solo-time-gate  the same prompts one at a time on D0 (QWEN_FAST_SOLO_LANE=1)
# Product: the median round time per live count (the design assumes the WHOLE 64-row trace runs when only two or three users are live),
# and what D0 gives a lone coding user: tokens per round and tok/s against the engines it replaces, printed as one line
# ("D0 vs per-request engines at 4096: X vs Y tok/s"). The design's F (a solo round) is D0's median round; T3 needs F <= 6.67 x tau.
# SOFT: a failing arm is data; the window goes on.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card lanes window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it
# over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lanes and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image L0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record as in L1.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 3-8 min plus 3-8 min of streams (the ladders' 2,400 tokens 1-3 min; a
# lone user 1,024 tokens at 25-150 tok/s, four times, 3-6 min): 45-100 min for five arms. Step limit 380 min; worst case 310 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lanes-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=round-timing
C2_GATE_JIT=record
